=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play dns/failed-save -----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: dns/failed-save$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13; /etc/resolv.conf is a file$
# dhcpcd wrote from eth0's lease, naming 192.0.2.1 and$
# example.net. hardn.yml lists 192.0.2.54, 2001:db8::54.$
# hardn.yml is immutable (chattr +i), so a change that saves it$
# fails, and the change is rolled back.$
$
# DNS Configuration ############################################$
$
# Current DNS Configuration ------------------------------------$
$
   -  DNS Implementation   direct (/etc/resolv.conf)$
   -  Nameservers          192.0.2.1$
   -  Search Domains       example.net$
$
# Configured Nameservers ---------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameserver 1         192.0.2.54$
   -  Nameserver 2         2001:db8::54$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Configure DNS        Apply nameserver settings from con...$
   2) Add nameserver       Add a new DNS server to configuration$
   3) Remove nameserver    Remove a DNS server from configura...$
   4) Use Cloudflare DNS   Set nameservers to 1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1$
   5) Use Google DNS       Set nameservers to 8.8.8.8, 8.8.4.4$
   6) Use Quad9 DNS        Set nameservers to 9.9.9.9, 149.11...$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-6 or q]: 4$
$
# Use Cloudflare DNS ###########################################$
$
# DNS Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameservers          1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1$
   -  Search Domains       example.net$
  [ ] dhcpcd may rewrite /etc/resolv.conf on a lease$
$
   -  Set the nameservers$
      /etc/resolv.conf$
      @@ -1,3 +1,4 @@$
       # Generated by dhcpcd from eth0.dhcp$
       search example.net$
      -nameserver 192.0.2.1$
      +nameserver 1.1.1.1$
      +nameserver 1.0.0.1$
$
   -  Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
      @@ -1,5 +1,5 @@$
       # hardn's configuration (web-01.example.net)$
       username: alice$
       nameservers:$
      -  - "192.0.2.54"$
      -  - "2001:db8::54"$
      +  - "1.1.1.1"$
      +  - "1.0.0.1"$
$
  Use Cloudflare DNS? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Set the nameservers     Done$
  [ ] Save the configuration  Failed PERMISSION_DENIED$
$
# Operation Failed$
# Saving /etc/hardn/hardn.yml failed$
$
  [ ] Set the nameservers     Rolled back$
$
  Check the log file at /var/log/hardn.log for details$
$
# DNS Configuration ############################################$
$
# Current DNS Configuration ------------------------------------$
$
   -  DNS Implementation   direct (/etc/resolv.conf)$
   -  Nameservers          192.0.2.1$
   -  Search Domains       example.net$
$
# Configured Nameservers ---------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameserver 1         192.0.2.54$
   -  Nameserver 2         2001:db8::54$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Configure DNS        Apply nameserver settings from con...$
   2) Add nameserver       Add a new DNS server to configuration$
   3) Remove nameserver    Remove a DNS server from configura...$
   4) Use Cloudflare DNS   Set nameservers to 1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1$
   5) Use Google DNS       Set nameservers to 8.8.8.8, 8.8.4.4$
   6) Use Quad9 DNS        Set nameservers to 9.9.9.9, 149.11...$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-6 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: dns/failed-save$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Set the nameservers$
      /etc/resolv.conf$
$
   -  Rolled back from the journal$
      /etc/resolv.conf$
$

